SWEET Bluetooth: patch 0277 (sprint-bt 2026-11-09), boot-arg sweetbtromread=1 (default off): READ-ONLY controller witness for the controller-side Apple multi-advertising (0xfd48) work, docs/research/sprint-bt-fd48-firmware.md s.6. Pass R on the ROM controller before the patchram download: Read_RAM (opcode 0xfc4d, Address uint32 LE + Length uint8, returns Status + data [src: Cypress AN215184 Rev *A s.3.10]) probes at 8 addresses, then one 512 KiB window (start = boot-arg sweetbtromoff, default 0; review M2/M3) in 128-byte reads up to the first refusal or the patch base 0x1a0400, rows `BT ROM: d <addr> <hex>` (firmware bytes only in the gitignored run log), HCI trace quiet meanwhile; then the controller is power-cycled and re-probed so the download starts clean. Pass P after a verified download: 0xfd54 with the unused sub-opcode 0xee (status 0x01 = no 0xfd54 handler) and a 32-byte read of the patch head (host compares it with BCM.hcd). No write command is sent; every refusal is a GAP row and nothing stops the bring-up. 0xfd54 without an answer is followed by an HCI Reset check (review M1); every refusal is a BT GAP row. Review docs/reviews/sprint-bt-0277-review.md (SAFE WITH CONDITIONS; M1, M2/M3, L1 fixed). Mode 2 (sweetbtromread=2, added after bt-rom1 20261109T221218Z lost ~97 % of the mode-1 hex rows in the live USB log [obs]): the whole range 0..0x1a0400 into one kernel buffer (new file bsd/dev/sweet_bt_rom.c), no hex rows, progress every 256 KiB, an FNV-1a row over the bytes, served read-only by sysctl debug.sweetbtrom (a userland helper copies it to a file the host pulls). Applies after 0274.

